  ('152861836740643166', 'I''ve Got to Sing a Torch Song', 1933, 'Animation, Comedy', 'Tom Palmer', null, 'Sara Berner', null, 'Blackout gags and music, including the title song originated in the movie musical Gold Diggers of 1933. Hollywood figures caricatured include Tallulah Bankhead, Joan Blondell, James Cagney, Bing Crosby, Guy Kibbee, Zasu Pitts, Mae West, Bert Wheeler and Bob Woolsey, Ed Wynn, George Bernard Shaw, Mussolini, Ben Bernie, The Boswell Sisters and Greta Garbo, who does the "Dat''s all, folks!".', 'Blackout gags and music, including the title song originated in the movie musical Gold Diggers of 1933. Hollywood figures caricatured include Tallulah Bankhead, Joan Blondell, James Cagney, Bing Crosby, Guy Kibbee, Zasu Pitts, Mae West, Bert Wheeler and Bob Woolsey, Ed Wynn, George Bernard Shaw, Mussolini, Ben Bernie, The Boswell Sisters and Greta Garbo, who does the "Dat''s all, folks!".', 'https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w500/zhNeDIfm9Pdc2UaFlXXk1uc7c4u.jpg', 'tmdb:movie:161866'),
  ('798606255211483186', 'I''ve Got You, You''ve Got Me by the Chin Hairs', 1979, 'Comedy', 'Jean Yanne', 'Jean Yanne, Gérard Sire', 'Jean Yanne, Mimi Coutelier, Michel Duchaussoy, Daniel Prévost, Jacques François, Georges Beller, Micheline Presle, Jean Desailly', null, 'In this satire, a police detectiveis investigating the disappearance and kidnapping of the host of a television dance show. However, instead of finding his man, he is trapped into becoming a contestant on a children''s quiz show. What''s worse is that he becomes a very successful contestant.', 'In this satire, a police detectiveis investigating the disappearance and kidnapping of the host of a television dance show. However, instead of finding his man, he is trapped into becoming a contestant on a children''s quiz show. What''s worse is that he becomes a very successful contestant.', 'https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w500/6gSVfIodQjVbQh3XiS2j8qvZvWO.jpg', 'tmdb:movie:71629'),
  ('583955896413503522', 'I''ve Heard the Mermaids Singing', 1987, 'Comedy, Drama', 'John Pace, Tom Quinn, Jake Fry', 'Patricia Rozema', 'Sheila McCarthy, Paule Baillargeon, Ann-Marie MacDonald, Richard Monette, John Evans, Brenda Kamino, Patricia Rozema', 'R', 'Scatterbrained Polly gets a job as a secretary in Gabrielle''s art gallery. Polly aspires to be a professional photographer, and idolizes Gabrielle for her artistic ability. When Gabrielle rekindles an old romantic relationship with the younger painter Mary, Polly becomes jealous, and discovers Gabrielle isn’t exactly who she claims to be.', 'Scatterbrained Polly gets a job as a secretary in Gabrielle''s art gallery. Polly aspires to be a professional photographer, and idolizes Gabrielle for her artistic ability. When Gabrielle rekindles an old romantic relationship with the younger painter Mary, Polly becomes jealous, and discovers Gabrielle isn’t exactly who she claims to be.', 'https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w500/dDKTy24pQrMr2BnF7ec9vihCaCT.jpg', 'tmdb:movie:117233'),
  ('1098862712929557642', 'I''ve Loved You So Long', 2008, 'Drama', 'Jérôme Alméras, Philippe Claudel, Julien Zidi', 'Philippe Claudel', 'Kristin Scott Thomas, Elsa Zylberstein, Serge Hazanavicius, Claire Johnston, Frédéric Pierrot, Laurent Grévill, Lise Ségur, Jean-Claude Arnaud', 'PG-13', 'A woman struggles to interact with her family and find her place in society after spending fifteen years in prison.', 'A woman struggles to interact with her family and find her place in society after spending fifteen years in prison.', 'https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w500/14i0SnmWzgejS4ZRcBbzkvXD6dp.jpg', 'tmdb:movie:8276'),
  ('656577049387432971', 'I''ve Never Been to New York', 2019, 'Music, Comedy, Romance', 'Philipp Stölzl, Thomas W. Kiennast, Mirjam Wille', 'Philipp Stölzl', 'Heike Makatsch, Moritz Bleibtreu, Katharina Thalbach, Uwe Ochsenknecht, Michael Ostrowski, Pasquale Aleardi, Marlon Schramm, Mat Schuh', null, 'In the life of TV presenter Lisa, everything revolves around her talk show, celebrities and the ratings. There is just as little room for love as there is for her mother Maria. When the 66-year-old loses her memory after a fall in her apartment and wakes up in the hospital, she can only remember that she has never been to New York and sets off immediately. Lisa goes in search of Maria with her makeup artist Fred. She struck gold on a cruise ship that was just leaving for New York. As stowaways, the three have no choice but to earn the passage. While Fred is hired as an assistant by the Greek on-board magician Costa, Lisa and Maria have to work in room service. The crossing soon takes surprising turns for mother and daughter: Maria falls in love with the charming dancer Otto, who supposedly knows her from before, and Lisa takes a liking to the widowed statistician Axel Staudach, who is traveling with his son Florian.', 'In the life of TV presenter Lisa, everything revolves around her talk show, celebrities and the ratings. There is just as little room for love as there is for her mother Maria. When the 66-year-old loses her memory after a fall in her apartment and wakes up in the hospital, she can only remember that she has never been to New York and sets off immediately. Lisa goes in search of Maria with her makeup artist Fred. She struck gold on a cruise ship that was just leaving for New York. As stowaways, the three have no choice but to earn the passage. While Fred is hired as an assistant by the Greek on-board magician Costa, Lisa and Maria have to work in room service. The crossing soon takes surprising turns for mother and daughter: Maria falls in love with the charming dancer Otto, who supposedly knows her from before, and Lisa takes a liking to the widowed statistician Axel Staudach, who is traveling with his son Florian.', 'https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w500/nNmIkKRoOCK2w1Dnsx4svKEZSmo.jpg', 'tmdb:movie:525424'),
  ('1111380586828573804', 'I''ve Never Had A Hilda', 2014, null, 'Héctor Ortega, Andrés Clariond', 'Andrés Clariond', 'Verónica Langer, Adriana Paz, Noé Hernández, Fernando Becerril, David Gaitán, María Luisa Coronel, Anna Cetti, Marco Antonio Aguirre', null, 'Hilda, the new housemaid, brings about an awakening in the life of wealthy Mrs. Le Marchand, who recalls her revolutionary past, questions her frivolous present and experiences an identity crisis.', 'Hilda, the new housemaid, brings about an awakening in the life of wealthy Mrs. Le Marchand, who recalls her revolutionary past, questions her frivolous present and experiences an identity crisis.', 'https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w500/byKPr00tQWKZb43gPaYFEQM5FF0.jpg', 'tmdb:movie:264530'),
